-- IMPORTS form one chain (each module imports the one before it), because l4 checks a
-- module again for every path it is imported by. Names are visible down the chain. This
-- module draws on: ocar-nouns, ocar-01-definitions, ocar-02-03-term-termination.

-- O-Car rules, the supplementary clause on the collection and protection of personal data (the
-- last two pages of text, src:1141-1249). Quotations are generated from
-- ../../source/raw/opes-ocar.txt.
--
-- ITS VERSION. The heading of the document names Decisions 124/2019 and 17/2022 only. This
-- clause cites Decree 13/2023/NĐ-CP of 17/04/2023, so it was made on or after that date, by an
-- instrument the document does not name (fork F3). Whether it is part of a given contract is
-- an input (`the personal data clause is part of the contract`); a contract concluded before
-- 17/04/2023 that says it is, is declined.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED. Clauses 7(b) (processing ends within 72 hours of a request to delete), 9 (no
-- consent: no contract) and 10 (exercising certain rights ends the contract as if the
-- Policyholder had terminated it). Clauses 1-6 and 8 list data, purposes, methods, recipients,
-- risks and rights: inert, quoted by their headings only.

§ `The personal data clause`

